  "text": "Home /\nConsular Affairs /\nVisa-free travel /\nVisa-free entry for citizens of a number of European countries\nVisa-free entry for citizens of a number of European countries\nCitizens of 38 European states are eligible to enter Belarus without a visa via all international road and rail border crossing points on the State Border of the Republic of Belarus. Travellers may use any valid travel document and may remain in Belarus for up to 30 days from the date of entry. For citizens of Poland, Lithuania and Latvia (including holders of Latvia’s non-citizen status), the permitted stay is extended to 90 days from the date of entry.\nAndorra\nAustria\nBelgium\nBosnia and Herzegovina\nBulgaria\nCroatia\nCyprus\nCzechia\nDenmark\nEstonia (including stateless persons permanently residing in Estonia)\nFinland\nFrance\nGermany\nGreece\nHungary\nIceland\nIreland\nItaly\nLatvia (including non-citizens of Latvia)\nLithuania\nLiechtenstein\nLuxembourg\nMalta\nMonaco\nNorth Macedonia\nThe Netherlands\nNorway\nPoland\nPortugal\nRomania\nSan Marino\nSlovakia\nSlovenia\nSpain\nSwitzerland\nSweden\nUnited Kingdom\nVatican City\nTravellers may make use of this visa-free regime an unlimited number of times until December 31, 2026 inclusive. The total duration of visa-free stays must not exceed 90 days within a calendar year.\nThe visa-free entry regime previously applied at Belarusian airports remains fully in effect.\nForeigners arriving visa-free in Belarus will be able to transit, including through airport checkpoints, to third countries, except Russia.\nThis arrangement does not apply to holders of diplomatic, service, special and other passports equivalent to them. At the same time, holders of biometric diplomatic passports issued by EU member states can enter, leave and transit through the territory of the Republic of Belarus without visas in accordance with the Agreement between the Republic of Belarus and the European Union on the facilitation of the issuance of visas.\nMore detailed information is available on the website of the State Border Committee of the Republic of Belarus.\nBelarusian Diplomatic Missions abroad\nVideo\n����������� �������� �.��������� �� �������� ������� ������ ������������ ��� // Statement by Minister M.Ryzhenkov at the open debate of the UN Security Council\nBelarusian Vytsinanka has been inscribed on the UNESCO Representative List of Intangible Cultural Heritage\nII Minsk International Conference on Eurasian Security\n2023 in the history of Belarusian diplomacy\nHigh-level International Conference on Eurasian Security\nStatement by Foreign Minister Vladimir Makei at the 77th session of the UN General Assembly (September, 2022)\nForeign Ministry on Social Media\nContacts\n+375 17 327-29-22\n+375 17 355-51-65\n+375 17 215 86 45\nOfficial Internet Resources\nPresident of the Republic of Belarus\nMinistry of Information of the Republic of Belarus\nCouncil of Ministers of the Republic of Belarus\nCouncil of the Republic\nHouse of Representatives\nNational Agency of Investment and Privatization\nNational Center of Legislation and Legal Information\nNational Tourism Agency\nInformation export support website Export.by\nBelarusian Universal Commodity Exchange\nBelarusian Chamber of Commerce and Industry\nOfficial website of the Republic od Belarus\nBelarus TV\nRadio Belarus International\nDipservice\nBusiness network TradeBel\nNational Academy of Science of Belarus\nMinistry of Education of the Republic of Belarus\nMinistry of Natural Resources of the Republic of Belarus\nMinistry of Health of the Republic of Belarus\nMinistry of Economy of the Republic of Belarus",
